  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.AchievementsSpecialFile": "[pg]Achievements are saved in a special savefile so no matter what savefile you're on, any earned achievements will be added to that special savefile."
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.BowSkillReset": "Due to a bug where your bow skill got reset after you've slain Kelt, your bow skill got reset. Fortunately, this is now fixed. As a compensation, your bow skill is now instantly set to max!"
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.CautionHeading": "<b><u>CAUTION</u></b>"
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.EnjoyRevampMod": "[pg]Without further ado, enjoy everything CoC Revamp Mod has to offer!"
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.EquipmentReclassified": "Due to a bit of restructuring regarding equipment, any reclassified equipment (eggshell shield and fur loincloth) that was equipped are now unequipped."
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.ImportingVanillaSave": "\nIt appears that you are importing your save from vanilla CoC."
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.LethiceRelease": "Due to the official release of Lethice, you can now fight her again! Be prepared to face the Drider Incubus and Minotaur King beforehand!"
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.PlanningToSaveOver": "[pg]If you're planning to save over your original save file, please stop to think. If you overwrite the save file from original game, it will no longer be backwards compatible with the original CoC."
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.SeparateSaveSlots": "[pg]I suggest you create separate save files. I recommend you use slots 10-14 for saving your progress in this mod."
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.SomeAchievementsAgain": "[pg]Some achievements, however, will require you to do it again."
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.Version08Achievements": "Starting in version 0.8 of this mod, achievements are now awarded. To ensure that you don't have to go through scenes again on new savefile, achievements will be awarded depending on flags."
  "Scenes.Camp.PromptSaveUpdate.Version13FurColor": "Starting in version 1.3 of the mod, fur color is now separate from hair color. So as a one-time offer, you can now choose fur color!"
