  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.Shoot": "Exercising your inalienable rights as a free [man], you discharge your firearm straight into the sky. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.Damage": "[b:({0})]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.Yeehaw": "[pg]Yeehaw! Gods bless Amaretha!",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.ShootAgain": "Once again employing your god-given rights, you discharge your firearm into the sky. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.Falls": "[pg]Succumbing to your might, [b:(monster.MarethSky)] falls to the ground, unable to fight.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.AskRape": "[pg]Do you rape it?",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.RapeStartCock": "You strip off all covering, excited to claim the spoils of your victory. The sky looks on in horror as you approach, your [cock] already rigid from gunfire",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.RapeStartVagina": "You strip off all covering, excited to claim the spoils of your victory. The sky looks on in horror as you approach, your [vagina] glistening in preparation",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.RapeStartNone": "You strip off all covering, excited to claim the spoils of your victory. The sky looks on in horror as you approach, your anus ominously clenching to the rhythm of Star Spangled Banner",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.RapeDemand": ". You pull its face to your nethers, demanding service.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.CompliesWithCamp": "[pg]Apprehensive though it may be, the Marethian sky complies, licking your {0}. The instant its tongue makes contact, you shudder. A feeling of euphoria passes over you, and you're gleeful to receive the treatment you deserve around here. Certain other people could learn a thing or two from this, you feel, glancing around your camp accusingly. You grind your hips forward, pressing yourself against the sky for more. It hesitates, ever unsure of this exchange, but gives into your demands.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.Complies": "[pg]Apprehensive though it may be, the Marethian sky complies, licking your {0}. The instant its tongue makes contact, you shudder. A feeling of euphoria passes over you, and you're gleeful to receive the treatment you deserve around here. You grind your hips forward, pressing yourself against the sky for more. It hesitates, ever unsure of this exchange, but gives into your demands.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.FinalCock": "[pg]The sky opens up to you, engulfing your [cock] in its entirety. You pump your hips energetically now, immersed in the act. The swirling vortex of stimulation works every point of contact you could possibly register. Groaning in bliss, you bring your [weapon] up and start firing wildly into the air, hollering as boisterously as your lungs can muster.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.FinalVagina": "[pg]The sky slips its serenely sky-like tongue deep into your folds. You pump your hips energetically now, immersed in the act. The swirling vortex of stimulation works every point of contact you could possibly register. Groaning in bliss, you bring your [weapon] up and start firing wildly into the air, hollering as boisterously as your lungs can muster.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.FinalNone": "[pg]The sky slips its serenely sky-like tongue deep into your depths. You pump your hips energetically now, immersed in the act. The swirling vortex of stimulation works every point of contact you could possibly register. Groaning in bliss, you bring your [weapon] up and start firing wildly into the air, hollering as boisterously as your lungs can muster.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Sky.Bless": "[pg]God bless this land.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.Prompt": "Would you like to hang the skull of an imp onto wall? ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.Current": "There {0} currently {1} hung on your wall.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.Full": "There is no room; you have already hung a total of 100 imp skulls! No imp shall dare approaching you at night!",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.Hang": "You hang the skull of an imp on the wall. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.HangCount": "There {0} currently {1} hung on your wall.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.Inspect1": "You wander over to your camp wall in a slightly sentimental mood. You've been in Mareth for some time, and the wall is a testament to your survival.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.InspectOne": "[pg]You walk right up to the single imp skull mounted on your wall and stare it in the eyes.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.InspectFew": "[pg]The imp skulls you've mounted on your wall are still somewhat sparse, but you can take a certain amount of satisfaction in them nonetheless.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.InspectMany": "[pg]They dot the tops of your palisades, pale and sun-bleached, silent watchers.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.InspectWall": "[pg]A veritable wall of bone surrounds the wooden one.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Skulls.InspectEnd": "[pg]After a moment, you find a seat and simply take some time to watch them. It might not be the most productive use of your time, but it feels good to appreciate your work.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.AdmireSkulls": "Admire Skulls",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.AddImpSkull": "AddImpSkull",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Shoot": "Shoot",
  "Scenes.Camp.BadEndGIANTBALLZ.ReductoPaste": "You smear the foul-smelling paste onto your [sack]. It feels cool at first but rapidly warms to an uncomfortable level of heat.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.BadEndGIANTBALLZ.ScrotumShift": "You feel your scrotum shift, shrinking down along with your [balls]. Within a few seconds the paste has been totally absorbed and the shrinking stops. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.TooExhausted": "You are too exhausted to work on your camp wall!",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.FirstPrompt": "A feeling of unrest grows within you as the population of your camp is growing. Maybe it's time you build a wall to secure the perimeter?[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.Continue": "You can continue work on building the wall that surrounds your camp.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.Segments": "Segments complete: {0}/5[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.Cost": "[pg]It will cost 50 nails, 50 stones and 100 wood to work on a segment of the wall.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.NotEnough": "[pg][b:Unfortunately, you do not have sufficient resources.]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.Learn": "You pull out a book titled \"Carpenter's Guide\" and flip it's pages until you come across instructions on building a wall. You spend a few minutes looking at the instructions and memorize the procedure.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.Remember": "You remember the procedure for building a wall.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.BuildText": "[pg]You dig four holes, [if (metric) {fifteen centimeters deep and thirty centimeters|six inches deep and one foot}] wide each, before putting up wood posts, [if (metric) {three and a half meters high and a third of a meter|twelve feet high and one foot}] thick each. You take some wood from your supplies, then saw and cut it into planks before nailing them to the wooden posts.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.HelpersAssist": " {0} assist you with building the wall, helping to speed up the process and making the construction less fatiguing.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.HelperAssist": " {0} assists you with building the wall, helping to speed up the process and making the construction less fatiguing.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.OneHour": "[pg]Thanks to your assistants, the construction takes only one hour!",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.TwoHours": "[pg]Thanks to your assistant, the construction takes only two hours.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.Daunting": "[pg]It's a daunting task but you eventually manage to finish building a segment of the wall for your camp!",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.Easy": "[pg]It's an easy task but you eventually manage to finish building a segment of the wall for your camp!",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.Done": "[pg][b:Well done! You have finished the wall! You can build a gate and decorate wall with imp skulls to further deter whoever might try to come and rape you.]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.GateLearn": "You pull out a book titled \"Carpenter's Guide\" and flip pages until you come across instructions on how to build a gate that can be opened and closed. You spend minutes looking at the instructions and memorize the procedures.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.GateText": "[pg]You take the wood from supplies, saw the wood and cut them into planks before nailing them together. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.GatePrompt": "You can build a gate to further secure your camp by having it closed at night.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.GateCost": "[pg]It will cost 100 nails, 100 stones and 100 wood to build a gate.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Wall.GateDone": "[pg]You eventually finish building the gate.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.BuildWall": "Build Wall",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.BuildGate": "Build Gate",
  "Scenes.Camp.BadEndGIANTBALLZ.ButtonShouldra": "Shouldra",
  "Scenes.Camp.Statues.One": "Looking around the perimeter of your camp you spy a single marble imp statue. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Statues.Many": "Dotted around and on the wall that surrounds your camp you spy {0}. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.BadEndGIANTBALLZ.RathazulArrives": "You shout as loud as you can to call Rathazul. Your call is answered as the alchemist walks up to you.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.BadEndGIANTBALLZ.RathazulHelps": "[say: My, my... Look at yourself! Don't worry, I can help, ] he says. He rushes to his alchemy equipment and mixes ingredients. He returns to you with a Reducto.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.BadEndGIANTBALLZ.RathazulRubsPaste": "He rubs the paste all over your massive balls. It's incredibly effective.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.BadEndGIANTBALLZ.RathazulAdvice": "[say: Try not to make your balls bigger. If it happens, make sure you have Reducto,] he says. He returns to his alchemy equipment, working on who knows what.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.IsabellaCampsite": "Your campsite got a lot more comfortable once Isabella moved in. Carpets cover up much of the barren ground, simple awnings tied to the rocks provide shade, and hand-made wooden furniture provides comfortable places to sit and sleep. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.SimpleCampsite": "Your campsite is fairly simple at the moment. Your tent and bedroll are set in front of the rocks that lead to the portal. You have a small fire pit as well. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.LivedInCampsite": "Your campsite is starting to get a very 'lived-in' look. The fire-pit is well defined with some rocks you've arranged around it, and your bedroll and tent have been set up in the area most sheltered by rocks. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.ComfyCampsite": "Your new home is as comfy as a camp site can be. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.FirePitIs": "The fire-pit is ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.FirePitAndTentAre": "The fire-pit and tent are both ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.SetUpPerfectly": "set up perfectly, and in good repair. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Artwork": "You've even managed to carve some artwork into the rocks around the camp's perimeter.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.CabinFrames": "There's an unfinished wooden structure. As of right now, it's just frames nailed together.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.CabinMissingDoor": "There's an unfinished cabin. It's currently missing windows and door.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.CabinMissingFloor": "There's a nearly-finished cabin. It looks complete from the outside but inside, it's missing flooring.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.CabinNearEdge": "Your cabin is situated near the edge of camp.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.NurseryFuture": "Marble has built a fairly secure nursery amongst the rocks to house your future children.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.NurseryKids": "Marble has built a fairly secure nursery amongst the rocks to house your {0}.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.DefenseCanopy": "A thorny tree has sprouted near the center of the camp, growing a protective canopy of spiky vines around the portal and your camp. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.WallSmall": "A thick wooden wall has been erected to provide a small amount of defense. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.WallSome": "Thick wooden walls have been erected to provide some defense. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.WallFull": "Thick wooden walls have been erected; they surround one half of your camp perimeter and provide good defense, leaving the other half open for access to the stream. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.WallGate": "A gate has been constructed in the middle of the walls; it gets closed at night to keep any invaders out. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Skulls.One": "A single imp skull has been mounted near the gateway",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Skulls.Few": "Few imp skulls have been mounted near the gateway",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Skulls.Several": "Several imp skulls have been mounted near the gateway",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Skulls.Many": "Many imp skulls decorate the gateway and wall, some even impaled on wooden spikes",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.SkullsCountOne": " to serve as deterrence. There is currently one skull. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.SkullsCountMany": " to serve as deterrence. There are currently {0}. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.SimpleTraps": "You have a number of traps surrounding your makeshift home, but they are fairly simple and may not do much to deter a demon. ",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Portal": "The portal shimmers in the background as it always does, looking menacing and reminding you of why you came.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.AntKids": " Really close to it there is a small entrance to the underground maze created by your ant children. And due to Phylla wish from time to time one of your children coming out this entrance to check on the situation near portal. You feel a little more safe now knowing that it will be harder for anyone to go near the portal without been noticed or... if someone came out of the portal.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Rookery.One": "There's a smallish harpy nest that your daughter has built up with rocks piled high near the fringes of your camp. It's kind of pathetic, but she seems proud of her accomplishment.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Rookery.Small": "There's a growing pile of stones built up at the fringes of your camp. It's big enough to be considered a small hill by this point, dotted with a couple small harpy nests just barely big enough for two.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Rookery.Medium": "The harpy rookery at the edge of camp has gotten pretty big. It's taller than most of the standing stones that surround the portal, and there's more nests than harpies at this point. Every now and then you see the four of them managing a boulder they dragged in from somewhere to add to it.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Rookery.Large": "The rookery has gotten quite large. It stands nearly two stories tall at this point, dotted with nests and hollowed out places in the center. It's surrounded by the many feathers the assembled harpies leave behind.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Rookery.Giant": "A towering harpy rookery has risen up at the fringes of your camp, filled with all of your harpy brood. It's at least three stories tall at this point, and it has actually begun to resemble a secure structure. These harpies are always rebuilding and adding onto it.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Rookery.Massive": "A massive harpy rookery towers over the edges of your camp. It's almost entirely built out of stones that are fit seamlessly into each other, with many ledges and overhangs for nests. There's a constant hum of activity over there day or night.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Rookery.Immense": "An immense harpy rookery dominates the edge of your camp, towering over the rest of it. Innumerable harpies flit around it, always working on it, assisted from below by the few sisters unlucky enough to be flightless.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Build": "Build",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.ReadCodex": "Read Codex",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.ChangeMagic": "Change Magic",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.MagicBW": "Black&White",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.MagicTF": "Terr. Fire",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Cabin": "cabin",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.Bedroll": "bedroll",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.EmberCrusade": "Since Ember began {0} 'crusade' against the minotaur population, skulls have begun to pile up on either side of the entrance to {1} den. There're quite a lot of them.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.HolliTree": "On the outer edges, half-hidden behind a rock, is a large, very healthy tree. It grew fairly fast, but seems to be fully developed now. Holli, Marae's corrupt spawn, lives within.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.AmilyBedding": "A surprisingly tidy nest of soft grasses and sweet-smelling herbs has been built close to your {0}. A much-patched blanket draped neatly over the top is further proof that Amily sleeps here. She changes the bedding every few days, to ensure it stays as nice as possible.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.AmilyBeddingHolli": "Amily has relocated her grass bedding to the opposite side of the camp from the strange tree; every now and then, she gives it a suspicious glance, as if deciding whether to move even further.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.NieveSnowmanOne": "A somewhat crude snowman stands in the camp, constructed by Nieve and your child in a bout of play.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.NieveSnowmanMany": "A somewhat crude snowman stands in the camp, constructed by Nieve and your children in a bout of play.[pg]",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.HungerLoud": "<b>You have to eat something; your stomach is growling loudly. </b>",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.HungerPainful": "<b>You have to eat something; your stomach is growling painfully. </b>",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.HungerThin": "<b>You are getting thinner and you're losing muscles. </b>",
  "Scenes.Camp.Desc.HungerStarving": "<b>You are getting weaker due to starvation. </b>",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Egg": "Egg",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Tree": "Tree",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Plant": "Plant",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Void": "Void",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Snow": "Snow",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.SnowOdd": "[pg]There's some odd snow here that you could do something with...",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Snowman": "[pg]You have a [snowman] here that seems like it could use a little something...",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.Challenge": "Challenge",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.ChallengeTeleport1": "You step through the portal, and feel as if you're moving through space at unbelievable speeds.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.ChallengeTeleport2": "[pg]Light around you bends and twists, the sound warping and morphing as you are dematerialized.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.ChallengeTeleport3": "[pg]In the blink of an eye, you vanish.",
  "Scenes.Camp.Actions.ChallengeMissing": "[pg]The way to the Tower's summit is not available yet.",
}
